      "lineNbr": 745,
      "author": {
        "id": 1019013
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-10T14:52:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Rust question) Overlay doesn\u0027t need to be recovered because we wouldn\u0027t use it any further. Do you keep copies for both fdt and overlay and restore them to keep the promise in the SAFETY comment?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 745,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 745,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "24b71f8a2a2b388a76019bfbb1cf860bf5daf42e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d4db0dec_6f88b99f",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/fdt.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 745,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-10T16:27:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, recovering the overlay is not a must in our case, but that highly depends on existing use of it. I thought it\u0027s always better to do a clean recovery.",
      "parentUuid": "7f17c0e3_d68ed3ab",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 745,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 745,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "24b71f8a2a2b388a76019bfbb1cf860bf5daf42e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2dd8ad56_0dff7ebd",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/fdt.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 745,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-11T07:53:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we\u0027ve decided to restore the overlay on error, why not make that a no-op by `fdt.apply_overlay(backup_overlay)`?",
      "parentUuid": "d4db0dec_6f88b99f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 745,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 745,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "24b71f8a2a2b388a76019bfbb1cf860bf5daf42e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5494459e_45c32d15",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/fdt.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 745,
      "author": {
        "id": 1019013
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-11T12:29:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AFAIK, `libfdt` implementation is to modify both base `fdt` and overlay `fdt` and don\u0027t recover them in error state. So I think that current behavior looks OK for me -- Our `libfdt` simply follows native libraries behavior, and our Rust code ensures safety.",
      "parentUuid": "2dd8ad56_0dff7ebd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 745,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 745,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "24b71f8a2a2b388a76019bfbb1cf860bf5daf42e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "46af00dd_04d48ec3",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/fdt.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 745,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-11T13:01:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, my point was: if `libfdt` is going to modify the DTBO we pass to it, why not pass the copy instead of the original? That way, we don\u0027t care about `fdt_apply_overlay` corrupting its input DTBO because we\u0027re discarding it when returning from `apply_debug_policy` anyway, and don\u0027t need to do any clean-up of the DTBO on error.",
      "parentUuid": "5494459e_45c32d15",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 745,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 745,
        "endChar": 60
      },
